{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1194097-seed-of-an-idea-regalia-of-thorns","id":1194097,"title":"Seed of an Idea: Regalia of Thorns","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Changeling: The Lost"],"posts":[{"date":"2018-03-10T17:32:00-08:00","id":1194097,"title":"Seed of an Idea: Regalia of Thorns","content":"This idea first firmed when the spoilers for 2E were the Underhill model of the game, and Seemings were defined by how they escaped Arcadia. At that point there was some discussion of how Loyalists could be technically their own Seeming, since they have a united way of leaving Arcadia too (their Master's behest, having embraced their Keeper's rule). This in turn led to the idea that Loyalists could have their own Contract associated with them.<br /> <br /> Now obviously, Seeming exist independently of how one leaves Arcadia (though that can be a factor depending on a specific character's narrative), but the idea I was playing with back then I think still has some potential merit. The &quot;Regalia of Thorns&quot; would in this model make up for Loyalists' lack of access to Court Contracts (unless of course they join as a spy). In theory other Changelings could learn these Contracts too, but invoking them puts their Clarity through the meat grinder and can draw Keeper &amp; Huntsmen attention.<br /> <br /> The &quot;Regalia of Thorns&quot; in part would draw on the Contract of Thorns and Brambles from 1E, wielding the thorns of the Hedge itself to entrap and to rend souls. In addition it grants Loyalist Changelings the authority to call upon Fetches and even Huntsmen in their masters' Name, even create temporary Fetches themselves.<br /> <br /> <br /> Do you think this is worth further creative work, and seeing how the mechanics would hypothetically play out? Or do you see glaring conceptual problems I haven't considered?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-10T18:21:21-08:00","id":1194110,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1194097-seed-of-an-idea-regalia-of-thorns#post1194097\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do you think this is worth further creative work, and seeing how the mechanics would hypothetically play out? Or do you see glaring conceptual problems I haven't considered?</div> </div> </div> </div>Stolen tokens and Contracts of the Shield cover a lot of the conceptual ground not already addressed somewhat by Goblin Contracts.<br /> <br /> I feel like if you want to make a thing to fill the void of Courtlessness among True Loyalists that isn't just &quot;they're better-resourced&quot; then you'd be better-served doing as 1e suggested and giving them something mechanically identical to a Mantle from their Keeper, and if you want to represent a deleterious Regalia (i.e. a thing that the True Fae keep physical copies of as manifestations of their power) then you'd be better off doing so as a rider on existing Regalia \u2014 maybe favored loyalists can share the benefits of their Keeper's Regalia at cost \u2014 but &quot;you have the social benefit of working for the same entity&quot; doesn't seem like it really merits a Contract.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}